    instructions: "- Hero fits the first viewport: headline max 2 lines, subtext max 20 words, CTAs visible. Shrink type before letting it overflow. Top padding max about 6rem.\n- Hero holds at most: one eyebrow or none, headline, subtext, one primary + one secondary CTA. Logo walls, pricing teasers and bullet lists go in sections below.\n- Full-height heroes use min-height: 100dvh, never 100vh.\n- With variance above 4, prefer split or left-aligned heroes over centered ones.\n- Eyebrow labels: at most one per three sections. No numbered section labels (01 / 02).\n- Each layout family appears once; eight sections need at least four families. Max two image/text zigzags in a row.\n- Bento grids have exactly as many cells as items, and 2-3 cells carry an image or tinted surface.\n- Nav fits one line at desktop, 64-72px tall.\n- Use CSS grid, not percentage flex math; write the under-768px fallback for every multi-column block.\n- Use cards only when elevation shows hierarchy; otherwise spacing and dividers. Lists over five items become groups, grids, tabs or accordions.\n- One CTA label per intent across nav, hero and footer; labels fit on one line.",
