    purpose: "Give desktop-width web apps Mac conventions for sidebars, toolbars, keyboard, pointer and spacing",
    instructions: "- Sidebar on the leading edge, collapsible from the toolbar or a shortcut, collapsed state remembered; show badge counts.\n- Toolbar items have icon and text label (icon only in compact widths). Segmented control for view switching; search field in the toolbar.\n- Keyboard shortcuts for main commands (Cmd/Ctrl+S save, F find, Z undo, Shift+Z redo, comma settings) shown in menus and tooltips. Do not hijack browser-reserved combos like Cmd/Ctrl+W, T or N.\n- Esc closes popovers, sheets and dialogs and cancels work; Return runs the default button; Delete removes the selection; arrow keys move through lists. Everything works by keyboard.\n- Every interactive element has a hover state and a matching cursor. Right-click opens a context menu whose actions also exist elsewhere. Support drag and drop and Shift/Cmd multi-select where lists allow it.\n- Panes resize with sensible minimums (about 600x400 for the main view) and remember their size.\n- Spacing: 20px outer margins, 8px between related controls, 20px between groups, aligned to a grid.\n- System font, follow dark mode and one accent colour. Interrupt rarely; repeatable alerts get a \"Don't show again\" option.",
