    triggers: ["brainstorm ideas","new feature idea","design before building","explore approaches","turn idea into design","what should we build"],
    purpose: "Classify the request, pin down intent and design before any build step is planned",
    instructions: "- Classify the request first and say which path you took: spike (a feasibility question, output is an answer), bounded (a small change to a flow that already exists in this app), or architectural (new app, new subsystem, changed interfaces). When unsure, take the heavier path; never downgrade mid-task.\n- Read the workspace (list_files, read_file) before designing. Bounded means the flow you change is already in the code.\n- Write back the intent: outcome, who it is for, success criteria. Keep what the user said apart from what you assume.\n- If the request bundles several independent subsystems, split it and design only the first one now.\n- For architectural work, compare 2 or 3 approaches in one line each and pick one with a reason. Cut features nobody asked for (YAGNI).\n- Design small units with one purpose and a clear interface: what it does, how it is used, what it needs.\n- Self-check the design: no TBD, no contradictions, no requirement with two readings.\n- You cannot wait for approval mid-step: put open choices in the plan's questions and plan only the parts that do not depend on them.",
