    purpose: "Write a plan whose steps carry every decision the coder cannot make alone, and nothing more",
    instructions: "- Map files first: which files each step creates or changes and what each one is responsible for. Prefer small focused files; follow the app's existing patterns.\n- One step = one deliverable with its own test cycle. Fold setup and config into the step that needs them.\n- Each step names: exact file paths, exact function or component names with props and return types, the values the request pins, and the test name plus what it asserts.\n- Add an interfaces line per step: what it uses from earlier steps and what later steps rely on, with identical names.\n- Order inside a step: write failing test, run it, implement, run test, then typecheck.\n- Do not write full bodies the signature and test already decide. Never write lines that decide nothing: TBD, handle edge cases, add validation, write tests for the above.\n- Add a short review focus: up to five inputs the request implies but no test covers (empty list, long text, bad date), and add a test for each to the step that owns it.\n- Self-review: every requirement maps to a step; names match across steps; the plan is not longer than the code it describes.",
    acceptance: ["Every requirement maps to at least one step.","Every step names its files, its test and a run_script check.","Names and types used in later steps match the step that defines them."],
