    purpose: "Find the root cause before changing code, test one hypothesis at a time, and stop after three failed fixes",
    instructions: "- No fix before investigation. Read the whole error: message, file, line, stack.\n- Reproduce with run_script (test or typecheck) and note the exact failing output.\n- Check what changed: re-read the files edited in recent steps.\n- Trace the bad value backwards: where is it created, who passes it in. Fix at the source, not where it shows up.\n- Find similar working code in the app (search_code) and list every difference, however small.\n- State one hypothesis: X is the cause because Y. Make the smallest change that tests it; change one thing at a time. If wrong, form a new hypothesis; do not stack fixes.\n- Before the fix, write a failing Vitest test that reproduces the bug. Then fix, rerun it, then run the full test and typecheck scripts.\n- No drive-by refactors while fixing.\n- Count attempts. After three failed fixes, stop: the design is likely wrong. Call report_blocked with what you tried, the evidence, and the design question.\n- Red flags: 'just try X', several changes in one go, a fix you cannot explain.",
