    instructions: "- Red: write one small Vitest test for one behavior, with a name that says the behavior. Use Testing Library queries by role or label; test real code, mock only what you must.\n- Run run_script test. Confirm it fails, not errors, and fails because the feature is missing, not a typo or bad import. If it passes, you are testing existing behavior: fix the test.\n- Green: write the simplest code that passes. No extra options, no features the test does not ask for.\n- Run the test again, then the whole test script, not just your file. Fix the code, not the test.\n- Refactor only while green: remove duplication, improve names. Do not add behavior.\n- If you wrote code before its test, rewrite it from the test; do not keep it as reference.\n- Before writing a test, name the code change that would make it fail. If none would, it tests nothing.\n- Report every failing test you saw, including ones you did not cause.\n- Skip only for config files and generated code.",
