    instructions: "- Before task_complete or any 'done', 'fixed' or 'passes': name the command that proves the claim, run it fresh with run_script, read the full output and failure count, then state the claim with that evidence.\n- Match claim to proof: tests pass needs a test run with 0 failures; build works needs the build script exit 0 (lint passing is not a build); type-safe needs typecheck; bug fixed needs the original symptom's test passing.\n- A run from before your last edit does not count. Rerun after the final change.\n- For a regression test, prove it can fail: it failed before the fix and passes after.\n- Requirements met means re-reading the step and checking each item, not just green tests.\n- Words like should, probably, seems to, looks correct mean you have not verified. Run the command.\n- If the output disagrees with the claim, report the real status with the output, or use report_blocked.\n- Report only what you ran. Never list a check you did not perform.",
    acceptance: ["Every success claim cites a run_script result from after the last edit.","The summary lists only checks that were actually run."],
