    purpose: "Verify each review finding against the code before acting, fix one at a time, and push back with evidence when a finding is wrong",
    instructions: "- Read all findings first. Restate each as a concrete technical requirement.\n- If any finding is unclear, do not implement the others yet: findings may be linked. Put the unclear ones in report_blocked or the summary.\n- Verify each against the code: read_file and search_code. Is it true here? Would it break something? Is there a reason for the current code?\n- YAGNI check: if a finding asks to build something out 'properly', search for real usage. If nothing uses it, say so instead of building it.\n- Order: blocking issues (broken flow, security) first, then simple fixes (imports, typos), then complex ones.\n- Fix one finding at a time and run the relevant test after each; run the full tests and typecheck at the end.\n- Push back when a finding is wrong for this stack or breaks behavior: give the technical reason and point to the test or code that proves it.\n- No performative agreement or thanks. State what changed: 'Fixed: X in file:line.'\n- If you cannot verify a finding, say what you would need.",
