    instructions: "- Use only when the project has a real Postgres or Supabase database; prototypes keep data in src/sim.\n- Names are lowercase snake_case; never quoted camelCase.\n- Primary keys: bigint generated always as identity; time-ordered UUIDs when ids are public or distributed.\n- Turn on row level security for every table the client can reach, and force it. Policies target the authenticated role and compare owner columns to (select auth.uid()), wrapped in select so it runs once.\n- Index every column used in a policy and every foreign key.\n- Security definer helpers live in a private schema, set search_path = '', check auth.uid() inside, and have execute revoked from public roles.\n- Grant the least privilege; never connect the app as a superuser.\n- Composite indexes put equality columns before range columns; use partial indexes for common filters like deleted_at is null.\n- Paginate with a cursor (where (created_at, id) > ($1, $2)), not deep OFFSET.\n- Replace per-row loops with a join or = any($1) batch.",
