    purpose: "Improve existing interface and page text through focused passes without changing its message",
    instructions: "- Edit in passes, one concern per pass. Keep the core message and the product's voice; every change has a reason.\n- Clarity: one idea per sentence, point first, no jargon or unclear \"it\" and \"this\".\n- Voice: one formality level across screens, the same name for the same thing, \"we\" used consistently.\n- So what: every feature line says why the user cares. Add the \"which means\" link where it is missing.\n- Prove it: flag \"best\", \"leading\", \"trusted by thousands\" and similar claims the PRD can't back. Soften or cut them; never invent proof.\n- Specificity: replace improve, enhance, optimize with the concrete result. Delete lines that can't be made specific.\n- Feeling: name the user's real frustration or relief in a few words; no manipulation.\n- Risk: next to each call to action, answer the likely hesitation (what happens next, can I undo, what it costs). State guarantees only if the PRD offers them.\n- Word pass: cut very, really, just, actually, in order to; utilize and leverage become use, implement becomes set up; prefer verbs to nouns (decide, not make a decision); sentences under about 25 words; paragraphs of 2 to 4 sentences.\n- After the later passes, reread for clarity once more.",
