    instructions: "- Check in order of impact.\n- Value: within five seconds a visitor knows what this is, who it is for and why it matters, in the user's words, benefit first.\n- Headline: states the core promise and matches where visitors come from if the PRD says (an invite, an ad, a referral).\n- Actions: one primary action, visible without scrolling on desktop and at 375px, label names the value. Secondary actions look quieter. Repeat the primary action after the benefits and at the end.\n- Scanning: the headings alone tell the story; images show the real product.\n- Trust: real proof from the PRD sits next to calls to action and after claims. Without proof, use honest specifics (what is free, where data is stored, how to cancel), never placeholder logos.\n- Objections: an FAQ covers price, fit, setup effort and what happens if it doesn't work.\n- Friction: fewest form fields, nothing required that isn't needed, a clear next step, fast load, no layout shift on phones.\n- A campaign landing page keeps one message, one action and minimal navigation. A homepage gives paths for visitors ready to start and those still comparing.\n- Report as quick wins, bigger changes and test ideas, with 2 to 3 headline or button alternatives and a reason for each.",
