    instructions: "- Before any page copy, write a short brief in docs/positioning.md (or the plan) drawn from the PRD. Copy tasks read it first.\n- Product: one-liner, what it does in 2 to 3 sentences, the category people would search for.\n- Audience: who it is for, the main use case, 2 to 3 jobs users hire it for.\n- Problem: the core pain, why current options fall short, what it costs the user.\n- Alternatives: direct competitors, different approaches, and doing it by hand.\n- Differentiation: what this does that alternatives don't, and why that matters to the user.\n- Objections: the top three with answers, and who the product is not for.\n- Switching: what pushes users away from today's way, what pulls them here, habits that hold them, worries about changing.\n- Language: words to use and avoid, plus a glossary so the UI names each thing the same way everywhere.\n- Voice: tone, style and 3 to 5 personality adjectives.\n- Proof: only what the PRD supplies; otherwise write \"none yet\".\n- Goal: the one conversion action.\n- List gaps as open questions; never present guesses as facts.",
